FINDING B1 SUMMARY:
  1. UL30 Polymerase (ACV & FOS):
     Zero-shot PLMs demonstrate a decisive +0.18 to +0.28 AUROC advantage over full
     multi-herpesvirus conservation. The PLM signal is NOT explained away by conservation.
  2. UL23 Thymidine Kinase (ACV):
     Multi-herpesvirus conservation achieves ~0.74, closely matching zero-shot PLMs (~0.74-0.75).
     This confirms the biological dissociation between the two targets:
     UL23 resistance is strongly driven by active-site conservation loss (TK inactivation),
     while UL30 resistance requires conformational/structural modeling beyond conservation.